Description: Detect spatially variable genes (SVGs) in spatial transcriptomics
  data, as used in the Spatial Transcriptomics Arena (STAr) platform. The
  package implements BOOST-GP (Li et al., 2021) <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btab455>
  and BOOST-MI, the modified Ising model (Jiang et al., 2022) <doi:10.1002/sim.9530>,
  together with SPARK, SpatialDE, and BinSpect, and provides wrappers that call
  the original software for nnSVG, SPARK-X, MERINGUE, Trendsceek, Seurat
  Moran's I, SOMDE, and SpaGCN. GEO and MC2 are provided for rank aggregation.
  The package also includes data filtering, normalization, binarization,
  neighbor construction, visualization, and performance metrics for SVG
  benchmarking. Methods like plot() and print() are available for
  convenience. This package utilizes the Armadillo C++ library for linear
  algebra and scientific computing <https://arma.sourceforge.net/>.
